1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:10.545
But when time pulls lives apart, hold your own.

2
00:00:10.545 --> 00:00:19.724
When everything is fluid, nothing can be known with any certainty.

3
00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:39.347
Hold your own hold it till you feel it there as dark and dense and wet as earth, as vast and bright and sweet as when all there is is knowing that you feel what you are feeling.

4
00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:44.585
Hold your own ask your hands to know the things they hold.

5
00:00:44.585 --> 00:00:59.905
I know the days are reeling past in such squealing blasts, but stop for breath and you will know it's yours swaying like an open door when storms are coming.

6
00:00:59.905 --> 00:01:02.731
Oh, time is an onslaught.

7
00:01:02.731 --> 00:01:04.750
Love is a mission.

8
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:09.191
We work for vocations until in remission.

9
00:01:09.191 --> 00:01:14.439
We wish wehad patience and given more time to our children.

10
00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:18.536
Feel each decision that you make.

11
00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:19.560
Make it.

12
00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.584
Hold it.

13
00:01:20.584 --> 00:01:22.120
Hold your own.

14
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.293
Hold your lovers, hold their hands.

15
00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:32.787
Hold their breasts in your hands like your hands were their bra.

16
00:01:32.787 --> 00:01:37.426
Hold their face in your palms like a prayer.

17
00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:39.281
Hold them all night.

18
00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:41.137
Feel them hold back.

19
00:01:41.137 --> 00:01:42.528
Don't hold back.

20
00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:43.920
Hold your arm.

21
00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:54.974
Every pain, every grievance, every stab of shame, every day spent with a demon in your brain giving chase.

22
00:01:54.974 --> 00:02:02.992
Hold, know the wolves that hunt you in time they will be the dogs that bring your slippers.

23
00:02:02.992 --> 00:02:08.985
Love them right and you will feel them kiss you when they come to bite.

24
00:02:08.985 --> 00:02:23.039
Hot snouts digging out your cuddles with their bloody muzzles hold nothing you can buy will ever make you more whole.

25
00:02:23.039 --> 00:02:33.756
This whole thing thrives on us feeling always incomplete, and it is why we will search for happiness in whatever thing it is we crave in a moment.

26
00:02:33.756 --> 00:02:56.659
And it is why we can never really find it, though it is why you will sit there with the lover that you fought for in the car you sweated years to buy, wearing the ring you dreamed of all your life, and some part of you will still be unsure that this is what you really want.

27
00:02:56.939 --> 00:03:01.860
Stop craving, hold your own.

28
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:26.367
But if you're satisfied with where you're at, with who you are, you won't need to buy new makeup or new outfits or new pots and pans to cook new exciting recipes for new exciting people to make yourself feel like the new exciting person you think you're supposed to be.

29
00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:32.020
Happiness, the brand is not happiness.

30
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.807
We are smarter than they think we are.

31
00:03:35.807 --> 00:03:40.355
They take us all for idiots, but that's their problem.

32
00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:44.580
When we behave like idiots, it becomes our problems.

33
00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.878
So hold your own.

34
00:03:45.878 --> 00:03:53.675
Breathe deep on a freezing beach, taste assalt of friendship, notice the movement of a stranger.

35
00:03:53.675 --> 00:03:56.599
Hold your own and let it be catching.
